From 112fea3c5f403e2309baea1567e1988b122f1ffd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UMP <ump@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/90] launcher: also follow Modrinth's own dependency links
 for Java mods

A mod's id in fabric.mod.json need not be its Modrinth project's name: BetterEnd and BetterNether require 'wover', which is World Weaver on Modrinth, so it was never found and the game stopped. The resolver now first asks Modrinth which projects the folder's jars (by SHA-1) require, and downloads those it lacks (Fabric API excepted: Horizon's own); a project is already there only when its own mod id is in the folder, not merely a library it carries (WunderLib). The id lookups stay for jars Modrinth doesn't know. Every skipped step says why.

Tested: BetterEnd + BetterNether + BoP + Enchanting Infuser -> World Weaver and 6 libraries; BoP + Waystones + Traveler's Backpack -> 5; second runs: nothing missing.
---
 launcher/src/browser/download.rs |  2 +-
 launcher/src/java_deps.rs        | 86 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 87 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

